    "notes": [
      "Offline GRLLM.beam_search with output_mode=compact, max_concurrency=1, and one prompt per call.",
      "Canonical E2E uses an outer perf_counter_ns and a final CUDA synchronization. It is sampled before stage instrumentation.",
      "Each canonical sample is a cold-cache call followed by an identical warm-cache call.",
      "Offline E2E excludes HTTP, SSE, serialization, and network round-trip overhead.",
      "Internal stage values come from a separate post-canonical diagnostic sample.",
      "Prefill and Decode are CUDA device-timeline intervals on one FIFO compute stream. Together with host_overhead they sum to diagnostic E2E. Decode includes device idle inside the Decode stage.",
      "Worker pipeline comes from a separate post-matrix process; formal E2E and post-canonical stage metrics remain unchanged."
    ]
  },
